      "reason": "end",
      "note": "No deviations from plan scope; both remaining beads (workspace-htgw header restructure, workspace-jzul Files tab) implemented, committed per-bead, pushed. All 9 pan-1232 beads now closed. Full frontend suite green (189 files / 1756 tests), frontend tsc + eslint clean.\n\nVerified deviations from bead wording (root-cause, not bandaids — all documented in commit bodies):\n\n1. Branch field. The header bead said activeAgent.branchName, but no branchName field exists on the Agent type. The branch lives at agent.git?.branch (GitStatus.branch) — how every other frontend surface reads it (CommandPalette, GodView/AgentCard, FocusView). Used the verified-correct field.\n\n2. Radius token. Header AC6 named var(--radius-md), but that CSS variable is undefined in the codebase (only --radius and --radius-sm exist as CSS vars; --radius-lg is referenced elsewhere but also resolves to nothing). The medium radius lives in the Tailwind theme (tailwind.config.js: md = calc(var(--radius) - 2px)), so the branch chip uses rounded-md — the working medium-radius primitive matching the AC's intent.\n\n3. formatSpend reused by exporting it from DrawerActiveAgent (bead's first-listed option) instead of duplicating.\n\n4. Files tab. DiffPanel has no 'files-only'/'compact' CONTENT mode (its modes are layout-only inline|sheet|sidebar), so the full inline DiffPanel is rendered per the bead's 'otherwise render the full DiffPanel'. DiffPanel is agent-scoped (it calls /api/agents/:id/diffs), so the Files tab scopes to the issue's canonical work agent via pickDefaultDrawerAgent — no new server endpoint added (AC4). Added an initial-fetch 'Loading files…' gate mirroring the standalone diff popout to avoid a misleading 'No completed turns yet' flash.\n\nMinor: commitlint emits a non-blocking scope-enum warning (scope 'drawer' vs allowed list) on both commits; commits landed fine. Amending is forbidden, so left as-is."
